'''Unit-13's False Evolution''' (第13号機 疑似シン化第3+形態（推定）, ''Dai 13 Gō-Ki Giji Shinka Dai-San+ Kētai (Suitē)'', '''Unit-13 Pseudo-Awakened Third Form+ (Estimated)''') is an [[:Category:EVA Angel Enemies|EVA Angel]] enemy that appears in the [[Neon Genesis Evangelion Collaboration Event]]. It was added in [[Version 8.7 Update#Update 8.7.5|Version 8.7.5]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Unit-13's False Evolution
|image = E 464.png
|appearance = [[EVA Unit-13 Strikes!]]
|money drop = 10,000¢ - 39,500¢
}}

==Enemy==
Unit-13's False Evolution is currently the most powerful EVA Angel from the Evangelion Collaboration, having massive amounts of damage and immunity to almost all status effects excluding [[Curse|curse]]. Along with its ability to knockback, freeze and weaken all Cat Units with a 100% chance. It also has a very long Omni Strike range of -3600~1200. Its negative range combined with its immunity to [[Wave Attack]]s makes cheesing not an option and/or a stressful challenge for many.

Thankfully, Unit-13 has low movement speed, low standing range and plenty of knockbacks. However, at 100% strength magnification, it has 4,000,000 HP and 100,000 damage (200,000 damage when strengthened!) and considering all [[Immune to Weaken|non-immune]] cats will get weakened, it effectively has 8 million HP! Combined with the peons in its [[We'll Meet Again (Merciless)|Merciless]] stage, this Angel can be considered a challenge for many.

==Strategy==
It is usually ill-advised to use meatshields against this monstrosity, as there are barely any fast ones that are immune to freeze or knockback. The only two relevant ones are [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Curling Cat]] and [[Sumo Cat (Special Cat)|Talented Riceball Cat]], who both stand no chance against this enemy due to its overwhelming damage, especially when strengthened. What's more, it can also use them as a stepping stone to wipe out all your units or even snipe the base, thanks to its absurd Omni Strike range.

The general strategy against this enemy is to either use rushers to slowly burst it down, or attack it from afar while triggering its attack as little as possible. The player must have a good timing on sending their units, so using most non-[[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|rusher]] [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rares]] is not a good idea, due to most getting killed in a single blow. If you want a unit that can can survive being hit and go on the attack back, it is required that they be [[:Category:Cats with Freeze Immunity|immune to Freeze]] or you have another attacker; otherwise, Unit 13's ability uptime of around 123% will make them worthless beyond absorbing damage.

If the player happens to own any [[:Category:EVA Angel Killer Cats|EVA Angel Killer]] Ubers, using the [[You Will Find Happiness (Combo)|You Will Find Happiness]] combo to boost them will allow this enemy to be much easier to deal with. With the combo, EVA Angel Killers will deal '''25x''' damage to and only take '''1/25''' damage from this enemy, allowing very large amounts of damage to be secured without getting eradicated in a single attack.

